  #<span class=sf-dump-protected title=\"Protected property\">original</span>: <span class=sf-dump-note>array:20</span> [<samp data-depth=2 class=sf-dump-compact>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>id</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-num>2</span>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>tour_id</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-const>null</span>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>nombre</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"17 characters\">Inca trail 5 days</span>\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>descripcion</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"130 characters\">The 5 day Inca Trail tour includes a  4 day trek along the trail and an additional day to explore Machu Picchu with Huayna Picchu.</span>\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>contenido</span>\" => \"\"\"
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1308 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;5-day Classic Inca Trail to Machu Picchu&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1308 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1308 characters\">&lt;p&gt;The 5 day Classic Inca Trail Tour to &lt;strong&gt;Machu Picchu&lt;/strong&gt; includes a 4 day trek along the trail and an extra day to explore Machu Picchu with &lt;strong&gt;Huayna Picchu&lt;/strong&gt; (additional cost). On the four-day trek to Machu Picchu, we learn about traditional Andean culture. The Inca Trail (Qapaq &amp;Ntilde;an in the native Quechua language), a 50 km stretch of authentic Inca stone pathways that once extended from Cusco to Machu Picchu, is one of the world&amp;#39;s most iconic outdoor excursions! Nothing beats the feeling of walking the Inca Trail that leads to the Lost City of the Incas just as the sun casts its first golden rays over the ancient stone buildings.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1308 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1308 characters\">&lt;p&gt;Walking the Inca Trail for 5 days with us means having a fully supported hike with porters and modern equipment accompanied by an experienced bilingual tour guide. Additionally, you are granted an extra day to discover Machu Picchu and the Huayna Picchu mountains (optional); all of this allows you to fully enjoy one of South America&amp;#39;s most popular hikes.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1308 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1308 characters\">&lt;p&gt;Join one of the best Machu Picchu hiking tours.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1308 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1308 characters\">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;Inca tril to Machu Picchu 2023&quot; src=&quot;https://pachamamaspirit.com/img/galeria/ciudadela-machupicchu.webp&quot; style=&quot;width:100%&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</span>
      \"\"\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>resumen</span>\" => \"\"\"
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;Summary of the 5-Day Trek on the Inca Trail&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sustainable Tourism:&lt;/strong&gt; At Pacha Mama Spirit, we are proud to promote and practice sustainable tourism by being environmentally conscious and supporting local communities. We are committed to supporting Sernamp in the 2023 Camino Inca by collecting trash and clearing the trail.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Service Level:&lt;/strong&gt; Superior all-inclusive service, additional horses for your gear and private transportation.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fitness Rating:&lt;/strong&gt; High demand: Some high altitude hikes or more strenuous activities, but accessible to most healthy travelers.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Age Requirement:&lt;/strong&gt; 12+ / All travelers under 18 years old must be accompanied by an adult.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equipment:&lt;/strong&gt; A professional bilingual tour guide, a cook, and porters.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodation:&lt;/strong&gt; 3x camping, 1x hotel.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meals: &lt;/strong&gt;4x breakfast, 4x lunch, 4x dinner, 4x afternoon tea.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transportation:&lt;/strong&gt; Private van transportation, 1x train (Expedition class).&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Camping Equipment:&lt;/strong&gt; We include double tents, sleeping bags, therma rest sleeping pads, pillows, and blankets on our trek.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Group Availability:&lt;/strong&gt; Minimum: 2 - Maximum: 8&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;/ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;h3&gt;Quick Itinerary:&lt;/h3&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day 01&lt;/strong&gt;: Cusco - Km 82 - Llullucha Pampa&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day 02:&lt;/strong&gt; Llullucha Pampa - Chaquicocha&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day 03: &lt;/strong&gt;Chaquicocha - Wi&amp;ntilde;ay Wayna&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day 04:&lt;/strong&gt; Wi&amp;ntilde;ay Wayna - Machu Picchu - Aguas Calientes&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day 05:&lt;/strong&gt; Machu Picchu - Cusco&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;/ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;Highlights of the 5 day Inca Trail:&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;A 4 day trek along the Inca Trail with a professional bilingual tour guide, a hiking chef, and super porters.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Walk the trail and visit Machu Picchu at a more relaxed pace.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;1-day tour of Machu Picchu.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Discover the Inca Route.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Guided tour of Machu Picchu.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Climb Huayna Picchu or Machu Picchu Mountain (optional).&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Includes extra porters for your personal belongings.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Personal camping equipment such as a sleeping bag, inflatable mattress, pillow, and blanket are provided.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;/ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;Meeting and Departure Point Before the Inca Trail:&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Departure point: Cusco - We pick you up at your hotel.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Departure time: 5:30am&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Information Point (Briefing): Our guide will visit your hotel 1 or 2 days before the hike.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Return point: Cusco - Our driver will drop you off at your accommodation.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2727 characters\">&lt;/ul&gt;</span>
      \"\"\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>detallado</span>\" => \"\"\"
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;Day 01: Cusco - Km 82 - Llullucha Pampa&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;p&gt;Early in the morning, we will pick you up from your hotel and take you in our private transport to the starting point of this trek on the &lt;strong&gt;Inca Trail&lt;/strong&gt;. We will begin at Piscacucho, also known as Km 82 (2,350 m.a.s.l). There, your guide will give you an informative talk about the visit to &lt;strong&gt;Machu Picchu&lt;/strong&gt; before crossing the checkpoint of the Inca Trail.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;p&gt;Then, you will walk along the &lt;strong&gt;Urubamba River&lt;/strong&gt;, visiting the Inca archaeological sites of Willca Racca and the huge Llactapata. After that, you will continue towards the canyon of the Cusichaca River, offering magnificent views of the Eastern Cordillera; in particular, the mountain of Veronica (5,850 m.a.s.l). You will have lunch in Chamana and then continue walking on the Inca Trail along the Cusichaca River, observing several stepped Inca agricultural terraces and irrigation canals until you reach the picturesque town of &lt;strong&gt;Wayllabamba&lt;/strong&gt;. After this, you will begin to ascend while appreciating various ecosystems on the way. Later in the afternoon, you will arrive at the town of Llullucha Pampa, a place that will be your first campsite (3,850 m.a.s.l). This is where the first camping will be set up.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Estimated walking time:&lt;/strong&gt; 7-8 hours&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Walking distance:&lt;/strong&gt; 17 km&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maximum elevation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; 3,850 m.a.s.l. (12,630 feet)&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum elevation:&lt;/strong&gt; 2600 m.a.s.l (8530 feet)&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Difficulty&lt;/strong&gt;: Moderate to challenging&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;/ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;Day 02: Llullucha Pampa - Chaquicocha&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;p&gt;After an early breakfast, you&amp;#39;ll continue the trek to Machu Picchu, ascending to the highest point of the trail: &lt;strong&gt;Abra Warmiwa&amp;ntilde;usqa&lt;/strong&gt; (Dead Woman&amp;#39;s Pass) at 4,200 meters above sea level. You&amp;#39;ll pass through the cloud forests of &lt;strong&gt;Yunkachimpa and Corral Punku&lt;/strong&gt;, which offer excellent views of the surrounding snow-capped peaks. From Warmiwa&amp;ntilde;usqa, you&amp;#39;ll descend into the &lt;strong&gt;Pacaymayo Valley&lt;/strong&gt; (3,300 m), where you&amp;#39;ll have a lunch break. Then, you&amp;#39;ll walk along the Inca Trail through the valley to reach the Inca ruins of Runkuracay, where a guided tour follows. After that, you&amp;#39;ll ascend and pass the second pass - &lt;strong&gt;Abra Runkurakay&lt;/strong&gt; (3,860m) walking on this &amp;quot;Royal Inca Trail&amp;quot; to the next Inca site - Sayacmarca. Along the way, you&amp;#39;ll pass by Yanacocha Lake. Finally, you&amp;#39;ll arrive at our second campsite - Chaquicocha (3,670 m).&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Estimated trekking time: 7-8 hours&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Trekking distance: 12 km Max. elevation: 4200 meters above sea level (12,630 feet)&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Min. elevation: 3500 meters above sea level (11,480 feet)&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Difficulty: Challenging&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;/ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;Day 03: Chaquicocha - Wi&amp;ntilde;ay Wayna&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;p&gt;Today, you&amp;#39;ll hike through beautiful subtropical vegetation and many important archaeological sites. Before reaching the first site, you&amp;#39;ll climb up the &lt;strong&gt;Phuyupatamarca&lt;/strong&gt; Pass (3670 m) and just behind it, you&amp;#39;ll see the well-preserved and complete Inka complex of Phuyupatamarca (3600 m.a.s.l.), which is located on top of a mountain and corresponds to its Quechua name that means &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;Town Above the Clouds&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot;. After a guided tour, you&amp;#39;ll have lunch there. Then, you&amp;#39;ll start a steep descent through a cloud forest that offers the opportunity to see beautiful orchids and different bird species on the way to our last campsite in &lt;strong&gt;Wi&amp;ntilde;ay Wayna&lt;/strong&gt; (2700 m). There, we&amp;#39;ll have a guided tour of the impressive archaeological complex of the same name, which consists of a religious sector, an urban sector, and an agricultural center with many stepped terraces. After that, dinner will be served and you&amp;#39;ll go to sleep to prepare for hiking the Inca Trail to Machu Picchu!&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Estimated hiking time: 5-6 hours&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Hiking distance: 10 km Max. elevation: 3670 m.a.s.l. (12,040 feet)&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Min. elevation: 2700 m.a.s.l. (8860 feet)&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Difficulty: Moderate&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;/ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;Day 04: Wi&amp;ntilde;ay Wayna - Machu Picchu - Aguas Calientes&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;p&gt;We start our walk early in the morning after breakfast. First, we climb ancient steps up to &lt;strong&gt;Inti Punku (the Sun Gate)&lt;/strong&gt; to see the sunrise over the long-awaited &lt;strong&gt;Machu Picchu&lt;/strong&gt; citadel. Then, we spend the rest of the morning exploring the Inka citadel on our own. For those interested, we meet in the town of &lt;strong&gt;Aguas Calientes&lt;/strong&gt; for lunch together. To get to Aguas Calientes, you can either take a slow descent (recommended for taking some lovely panoramic photos; takes about an hour) or a shuttle bus (approximately 20 minutes; costs $12 which is not included in the Camino Inca package). You spend the night in a comfortable hostel where you can enjoy a hot shower.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Estimated hiking time: 3 hours&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Hiking distance: 4 km Max. elevation: 2700 m.a.s.l. (8860 ft)&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Min. elevation: 2400 m.a.s.l. (7875 ft)&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Difficulty: easy to moderate&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;/ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;Day&amp;nbsp;05: Machu Picchu - Aguas Calientes - Cusco&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;p&gt;No hiking is expected on this day, just a ride as we take a shuttle bus after an early breakfast. The bus drops us off in front of the gates of the mysterious city of &lt;strong&gt;Machu Picchu&lt;/strong&gt; where we enter for the best early morning photo opportunities! Then, just enjoy a 2.5-hour guided tour of the so-called &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;Lost City of the Incas&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot;. Afterward, you have the opportunity to climb either Huayna Picchu peak (45 minutes up and the same time down, optional) or &lt;strong&gt;Machu Picchu mountain&lt;/strong&gt; (1 hour, 30 minutes up and down, optional) on your own for some panoramic shots of Machu Pichu. This Machu Picchu tour ends in the afternoon by descending to the town of Aguas Calientes where we take a train back to Cusco. Arrival in the afternoon.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"6194 characters\">&lt;p&gt;End of service! I hope you have enjoyed this longer trek of the Inca Trail!&lt;/p&gt;</span>
      \"\"\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>incluidos</span>\" => \"\"\"
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\">&lt;h3&gt;Includes in the Inca Trail:&lt;/h3&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\">&lt;ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Pre-trek briefing with your tour guide (our guide will visit your hotel one day before the trek).&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Private transportation to the starting point of the trail at Km 82.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Accommodation: camping (3 nights), hotel (1 night).&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Inca Trail permit and 2 entries to Machu Picchu.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Meals: 4x breakfast, 4x lunch, 4x dinner, 3x hot drinks in the afternoon (If you are vegetarian, please let us know in advance. The vegetarian food option has no additional cost!).&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Experienced bilingual tour guide (a group of up to 10 participants has 1 tour guide, a group of more than 10 participants receives 2 tour guides).&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Professional trekking chef.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Super Porters to carry food, camping equipment, cooking equipment, and 5 kg of each passenger&amp;#39;s personal belongings.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Camping equipment: Eureka Mountain double personal tents (3-person tent that allows for greater comfort and storage of backpacks).&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Inflatable mattress (Term-a-Rest mattress).&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;A sleeping bag (for up to -5&amp;deg;C).&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;One blanket per person.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;One pillow.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;A pair of hiking poles.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Travel bag (for your personal belongings).&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;A Caminata a Machu Picchu t-shirt.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Tables and chairs, kitchen tent with cooking equipment, dining and bathroom tents, and bottled gas.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;A shuttle bus from Machu Picchu to the town of Aguas Calientes.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Tourist train from Aguas Calientes (Machu Picchu) to Ollantaytambo.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Tourist bus from Ollantaytambo to Cusco.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;First aid kit that includes an emergency oxygen bottle.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\">&lt;/ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\">&lt;h3&gt;Not includes in the Inca trail:&lt;/h3&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"1766 characters\">&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</span>
      \"\"\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>importante</span>\" => \"\"\"
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;Inca Trail Advisory&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;p&gt;Working conditions of the porters. Every year, thousands of people hike the Inca Trail. They usually complete the 43 km trail in 4 days. For most of them, the journey is the experience of a lifetime and the realization of their personal ambitions. The satisfaction of having completed the hike and visiting the spectacular Inca city of Machu Picchu is hard to beat. However, this feeling is even better if you know that all the porters who help you along the way have been treated well and with the respect they deserve.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;p&gt;At &lt;strong&gt;Pacha Mama Spirit,&lt;/strong&gt; we don&amp;#39;t allow this kind of exploitation. We guarantee that our porters carry the amount allowed by Peruvian law.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;Inca trail camping:&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;p&gt;During the Inca Trail hike, we spend three nights camping with full service, which means that our camp staff will set up and take down the tents, cook, and perform all the camp chores for you - you only need to carry your backpack. There will also be dining and bathroom tents, and warm water bowls will be provided both in the morning and evening for washing up. On the last night, you will stay at a small hotel in Machu Picchu. All the hotels we use in Aguas Calientes are located within walking distance of the train stations.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;h2&gt;MOUNTAIN PASS 3XTE - Personal tents&lt;/h2&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;p&gt;The simplicity of the design meets expedition standards. The best features of Eureka&amp;#39;s camping and expedition tents are combined to create an extremely durable tent that sets up quickly. Designed with a focus on weatherproofing and durable coatings ideal for frequent use in cool and humid environments during the mid-to-late fall and early spring seasons.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;p&gt;Our tents are from the MOUNTAIN PASS 3XTE or DOITE EXPEDITION brand designated for 4 seasons. We have tents with a capacity for 3 people, however, we provide the tents for only 2 people. This way, we provide you with more space and comfort. In the case of a single traveler, we provide a tent with a capacity for 2 people. After each hike, we carefully check our tents and repair them if necessary!&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;h3&gt;Camping points of the Inca Trail:&lt;/h3&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;ul&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;First Night: Ayapata or Llulluchapampa.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Second Night: Chaquicocha.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Third Night: Phuyupatamarca or Wi&amp;ntilde;aywayna.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\"><span class=\"sf-dump-default\">\\t</span>&lt;li&gt;Fourth Night: Town of Aguas Calientes, please check the information in the &amp;quot;Accommodation in Machu Picchu&amp;quot; section.&lt;/li&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2475 characters\">&lt;/ul&gt;</span>
      \"\"\"
